operation getTitlePointerAt
input operation getTitlePointerAt titlesBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input operation getTitlePointerAt todoIndex CSignedInt64
input operation getTitlePointerAt titleCapacity CSignedInt64
output operation getTitlePointerAt COpaqueMemoryAddress
memory getTitlePointerAt heap no
async getTitlePointerAt no
purpose operation getTitlePointerAt "Return the start pointer for one title slot in the contiguous title array."
invariant operation getTitlePointerAt "The returned pointer is titlesBuffer plus todoIndex multiplied by titleCapacity."
invariant operation getTitlePointerAt "This operation is the *title-stride* half of the implicit `TodoEntry` record. The corresponding done flag for the same todoIndex lives at byte offset todoIndex in the sibling doneArray (stride 1). A future refactor that introduces `record TodoEntry { field done Bool, field title CNullTerminatedByteString }` plus `recordLayout TodoEntry column` would replace this pointer arithmetic with declarative field access; until that exists, every reader/writer of the two arrays must obey the same-index rule documented in `invariant main` (todo data shape)."
label startGetTitlePointerAt
call offsetCall math.multiplyI64
argument offsetCall left I64 todoIndex
argument offsetCall right I64 titleCapacity
run offsetCall
bind value titleOffset CSignedInt64 offsetCall
call pointerCall pointer.offset
argument pointerCall base COpaqueMemoryAddress titlesBuffer
argument pointerCall offset CByteCount titleOffset
run pointerCall
bind value titlePointer COpaqueMemoryAddress pointerCall
return value titlePointer

