operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer
input operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer targetBuffer COpaqueMemoryAddress
input operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer currentLength CSignedInt64
input operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer bufferCapacity CSignedInt64
input operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer keyCode TuiKeyCode
output operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer CSignedInt64
effect appendPrintableKeyToBuffer write memory.buffer
authority appendPrintableKeyToBuffer write memory.buffer
memory appendPrintableKeyToBuffer heap no
async appendPrintableKeyToBuffer no
purpose operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "Append one printable key to the edit buffer when there is room."
invariant operation appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "The target buffer remains null-terminated and currentLength never grows past capacity minus one."
warning appendPrintableKeyToBuffer "Only single-byte printable ASCII input (codepoints 32..126) is accepted. Multi-byte UTF-8 input, terminal paste blocks, control characters, and IME composition sequences are silently dropped here; supporting them requires a UTF-8 decoder and a separate paste-mode reader, neither of which exists yet."
label startAppendPrintableKeyToBuffer
storage local immutable oneStep CSignedInt64 1
# rationale: The inclusive ASCII printable range. 32 = ' ' (space, the lowest
# printable character) and 126 = '~' (tilde, the highest before DEL at 127).
# Bytes outside [32..126] are dropped — see the warning on this operation.
storage local immutable minPrintableKey CSignedInt32 32
storage local immutable maxPrintableKey CSignedInt32 126
call belowPrintableCheckCall math.lessThanCSignedInt32
argument belowPrintableCheckCall left CSignedInt32 keyCode
argument belowPrintableCheckCall right CSignedInt32 minPrintableKey
run belowPrintableCheckCall
bind value belowPrintable Bool belowPrintableCheckCall
branch if condition belowPrintable target skipAppendPrintableKey
call abovePrintableCheckCall math.greaterThanCSignedInt32
argument abovePrintableCheckCall left CSignedInt32 keyCode
argument abovePrintableCheckCall right CSignedInt32 maxPrintableKey
run abovePrintableCheckCall
bind value abovePrintable Bool abovePrintableCheckCall
branch if condition abovePrintable target skipAppendPrintableKey
call maxWritableIndexCall math.subtractI64
argument maxWritableIndexCall left I64 bufferCapacity
argument maxWritableIndexCall right I64 oneStep
run maxWritableIndexCall
bind value maxWritableIndex CSignedInt64 maxWritableIndexCall
call capacityCheckCall math.greaterThanOrEqualI64
argument capacityCheckCall left I64 currentLength
argument capacityCheckCall right I64 maxWritableIndex
run capacityCheckCall
bind value bufferFull Bool capacityCheckCall
branch if condition bufferFull target skipAppendPrintableKey
call storeKeyCall pointer.storeByte
argument storeKeyCall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress targetBuffer
argument storeKeyCall offset CByteCount currentLength
argument storeKeyCall value CSignedInt64 keyCode
run storeKeyCall
call incrementLengthCall math.addI64
argument incrementLengthCall left I64 currentLength
argument incrementLengthCall right I64 oneStep
run incrementLengthCall
bind value nextLength CSignedInt64 incrementLengthCall
call terminateBufferCall pointer.storeByte
argument terminateBufferCall buffer COpaqueMemoryAddress targetBuffer
argument terminateBufferCall offset CByteCount nextLength
argument terminateBufferCall value CSignedInt64 nulByte
run terminateBufferCall
return value nextLength
label skipAppendPrintableKey
return value currentLength

