operation main
input operation main console Console
output operation main Result ExitCode MainError
effect main read console.stdin
effect main write console.stdout
effect main read filesystem
effect main write filesystem
effect main open file
effect main close file
effect main allocate heap
effect main free heap
effect main read memory.buffer
effect main write memory.buffer
authority main read console.stdin
authority main write console.stdout
authority main read filesystem
authority main write filesystem
authority main open file
authority main close file
authority main allocate heap
authority main free heap
authority main read memory.buffer
authority main write memory.buffer
memory main heap yes
memoryAllocationSource main allocateDoneArrayCall
memoryAllocationSource main allocateTitlesArrayCall
memoryAllocationSource main allocateEditBufferCall
memoryAllocationSource main allocateLineBufferCall
async main no
purpose operation main "Run a heap-array backed keyboard todo TUI with JSON persistence."
invariant operation main "todo data shape: the active todos for indices [0, todoCount) are stored as two parallel heap arrays — doneArray (stride 1 byte; each cell holds byte value 0=open or 1=done, passed through CSignedInt32 only because that is the value type pointer.storeByte / pointer.loadByte accepts; the on-disk and in-memory storage is a single byte per todo) and titlesArray (stride titleCapacity bytes; each cell holds a CNullTerminatedByteString of at most titleCapacity-1 bytes plus NUL). Both arrays are allocated to length todoCapacity; the i-th todo's done flag is at pointer.offset(doneArray, i) and its title is at getTitlePointerAt(titlesArray, i, titleCapacity). Every reader/writer of `a todo` (renderTodoRow, saveTodosToJson, loadTodosFromJson, appendTodoFromEditBuffer, commitEditToSelectedTodo, toggleTodoAtSelectedIndex, deleteTodoAtSelectedIndex) obeys this same-index rule. Migrating to `record TodoEntry { field done Bool, field title CNullTerminatedByteString }` with `recordLayout TodoEntry column` would make the layout declarative."
invariant operation main "The selected index stays within the active todo range plus the add row while capacity remains."
invariant operation main "restoreCursorOnExit owns cursor visibility cleanup on every exit path; showCursor is idempotent and safe before hideCursor."
invariant operation main "After startup, every interactive mutation path (toggle, append, commit, delete) exits through persistTodosThenLoop; if saveTodosToJson succeeds, todos.json reflects the new todo state before the next render. Startup load mutates the arrays through loadTodosFromJson and does not route through persistTodosThenLoop because it is restoring already-persisted state."
invariant operation main "lineBufferBytes = 384 is the worst-case-safe bound for a JSON line emitted by saveTodosToJson at titleCapacity = 128: 2 * (titleCapacity - 1) escaped bytes (254) + 30-byte itemPrefixFormatText prefix + 4-byte item suffix + 1-byte c.fgets NUL = 289 bytes, rounded up to 384 for headroom. If titleCapacity grows, lineBufferBytes must grow with it or c.fgets will truncate an all-quote/all-backslash adversarial title on reload."
invariant operation main "lineBufferBytes (CByteCount) and lineBufferCapacity (CSignedInt32) are deliberately parallel scalars holding the same numeric value — lineBufferBytes is the malloc size and lineBufferCapacity is the c.fgets `count` argument. They MUST stay equal: a future edit that bumps one without the other will desync allocation and read length, silently truncating or over-reading. If SemanticScript later supports an explicit narrowing call from CByteCount to CSignedInt32, derive lineBufferCapacity from lineBufferBytes rather than carrying two constants."
invariant operation main "lineBuffer lifetime: allocated by allocateLineBufferCall before loadTodosFromJson and freed by freeLineBufferCall immediately after load completion. Unlike doneArray, titlesArray, and editBuffer (which live until quitProgram), lineBuffer is intentionally a short-lived scratch buffer for one-shot JSON parsing. The asymmetry is deliberate: quitProgram MUST NOT free lineBuffer again because it has already been freed; a use of lineBuffer after the loadTodosCall return is a use-after-free."
defer restoreCursorOnExit showCursor
deferRunOn restoreCursorOnExit all
label startMain
storage local immutable zeroValue CSignedInt64 0
storage local immutable oneValue CSignedInt64 1
storage local immutable todoCapacity CSignedInt64 128
storage local immutable titleCapacity CSignedInt64 128
storage local immutable doneFlagByteWidth CSignedInt64 1
storage local immutable titleByteWidth CSignedInt64 1
# rationale: visibleRows is 8 because the framed table plus status + help
# fits an 80x24 terminal with header room. todoCapacity 128 caps heap use
# under (128 * (1 + titleCapacity)) bytes ≈ 16 KiB.
storage local immutable visibleRows CSignedInt64 8
# rationale: lineBufferBytes is sized for the worst-case JSON-escaped line so
# reload never truncates a title the saver wrote. The bound is:
#   2 * (titleCapacity - 1)             max escaped title bytes
#   + len("{\"active\":1,\"done\":N,\"title\":\"") = 30 bytes prefix
#   + len("\"},\n") = 4 bytes suffix (the all-but-last item form is the longest)
#   + 1 byte NUL terminator written by c.fgets
# At titleCapacity = 128 the strict worst case is 2*127 + 30 + 4 + 1 = 289
# bytes; we round up to 384 to leave headroom for any future framing tweak
# in saveTodosToJson's itemPrefixFormatText. If titleCapacity grows, this
# value MUST grow with it — see the matching invariant on main.
storage local immutable lineBufferBytes CByteCount 384
storage local immutable lineBufferCapacity CSignedInt32 384
# rationale: list-mode key bindings — these are the raw bytes c.consoleGetch
# returns for non-extended keys, matching ASCII values:
#   13 = CR/Enter, 8 = Backspace, 32 = Space, 27 = ESC, 68 = 'D', 100 = 'd'.
# Arrow keys come through readTuiKey as normalized TuiKeyCodes >255 (see
# tuiKeyArrow* at module scope). Capital-D and lowercase-d both bind to the
# delete action so it works regardless of caps-lock / shift state.
storage local immutable keyEnter TuiKeyCode 13
storage local immutable keyBackspace TuiKeyCode 8
storage local immutable keySpace TuiKeyCode 32
storage local immutable keyDeleteUpper TuiKeyCode 68
storage local immutable keyDeleteLower TuiKeyCode 100
storage local immutable keyEscape TuiKeyCode 27
storage local immutable readyStatusText CNullTerminatedByteString "Ready."
storage local immutable loadedStatusText CNullTerminatedByteString "Loaded todos.json."
storage local immutable editStatusText CNullTerminatedByteString "Editing note."
storage local immutable savedText CNullTerminatedByteString "Saved."
storage local immutable saveFailedText CNullTerminatedByteString "Save failed; todos.json may be stale."
storage local immutable toggledText CNullTerminatedByteString "Toggled."
storage local immutable deletedText CNullTerminatedByteString "Deleted."
storage local immutable emptyIgnoredText CNullTerminatedByteString "Empty note not saved."
storage local immutable listFullText CNullTerminatedByteString "Todo array is full."
storage local immutable noTodoText CNullTerminatedByteString "No todo selected."
storage local immutable canceledText CNullTerminatedByteString "Edit canceled."
storage local immutable ignoredKeyText CNullTerminatedByteString "No action for that key."
storage local immutable goodbyeText CNullTerminatedByteString "\n  TaskForge TUI session saved.\n\n  todos.json is up to date.\n  Run taskforge_tui.exe from apps/taskforge-tui/build to reopen.\n"
storage local immutable quitSaveFailedText CNullTerminatedByteString "\n  TaskForge TUI session ended.\n\n  Save failed; todos.json may be stale.\n  Check file permissions and disk state before relying on it.\n"
storage local immutable allocationFailedText CNullTerminatedByteString "Could not allocate todo arrays."
storage local mutable todoCount CSignedInt64 zeroValue
storage local mutable selectedIndex CSignedInt64 zeroValue
storage local mutable topIndex CSignedInt64 zeroValue
storage local mutable screenMode ScreenMode ListMode
storage local mutable editLength CSignedInt64 zeroValue
storage local mutable statusMessage CNullTerminatedByteString readyStatusText
storage local mutable exitMessage CNullTerminatedByteString goodbyeText

